{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30253 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Amurensin is implicated in the biological activity of LNCaP cells through a series of molecular pathways that ultimately converge on the target cell. The evidence suggests that Amurensin acts as a target for Caspase-5, which is then targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid, all of which have a target relationship with LNCaP. This indicates that Amurensin may influence LNCaP through Caspase-5, potentially triggering apoptotic pathways. The shared involvement of Caspase-5 in these pathways suggests a common mechanism of action, possibly through the modulation of cell death processes. The integration of these targets highlights a potential role for Amurensin in modulating LNCaP cell behavior, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
